This article focuses on unimplemented features exclusive in the [[The Battle Cats Unite!|Nintendo Switch]] version of [[The Battle Cats]]. Since there are three versions of The Battle Cats Unite (Japan, Southeast Asia, and International), there may be slight differences on what may be unimplemented or available. It should be noted that The Battle Cats Unite is based off [[Version 6.10 Update|Version 6.10]] of The Battle Cats on launch. ''Updated as of October 10, 2026.''

==Unused Cat Units==
Though most units are present in-game, there are still plenty of units that cannot be obtainable between all three versions. The range of accessibility comes from full playability with slight modifications in the game or left with a few sprite sheets and data.

===Catburger===
Catburger is the only fully functional [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]] in this list, though it only has its Normal and Evolved forms. Originally implemented in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.5 Update|Patch 1.0.5]], it is possible that there would be a full international release back in 2021, but with sudden changes, left the release limited to Southeast Asia for Bandai Namco SEA to publish. Considering the poor reception of [[The Battle Cats POP!]], this may have been a factor into reconsidering the release, leaving Catburger left unused in its entirety. The current way to reinstate this unit is to modify one's save file using external third-party software.

===Li'l Cats===
There are unused spritesheets for most of the [[:Category:Li'l Cats|Li'l Cats]], suggesting they were meant to be unlockable through some different means similar to that of the [[:Category:Serial Code Cats|Serial Code Cats]] from mobile. However, there is no known working code to summon these units and only their spritesheets remain available. The only Li'l Cats to not have spritesheets are [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Bird Cat]], [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Fish Cat]], [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lizard Cat]], and [[Li'l Titan Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Titan Cat]].
