==Unused True Forms==
Every unused true form can be reinstated to the game via save file modification, hinting at one point they were considered since most of their forms are fully functional.

===Purchasable Special Cats===
Each of the [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]] that cost Cat Food to unlock has an unused [[True Form]] that has full functionality and can only be used when manipulating one's save file. The following cats have an unused True Form:
*[[Actress Cat (Special Cat)#Beefcake Cat|Beefcake Cat]]
*[[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)#Dancer Cat|Dancer Cat]]
*[[Mr. (Special Cat)#Hyper Mr.|Hyper Mr.]]
*[[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)#Ultimate Bondage Cat|Ultimate Bondage Cat]]
*[[Dom Cat (Special Cat)#Dark Lazer|Dark Lazer]]
*[[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)#Heavy Assault C.A.T.|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]
*[[Panties Cat (Special Cat)#Lollycat|Lollycat]]
*[[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)#Flying Ninja Cat|Flying Ninja Cat]]
*[[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)#Skelecat|Skelecat]]
*[[Samurai Cat (Special Cat)#Pastry Cat|Pastry Cat]]
*[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)#Riceball Cat|Riceball Cat]]
*[[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)#Gato Amigo|Gato Amigo]]
*[[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)#Loincloth Cat|Loincloth Cat]]
Since these True Forms go completely unused, any additions for anti-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] abilities that were reintroduced in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]], these purchasable Special Cats did not receive those changes. This leaves Hyper Mr., Skelecat, Pastry Cat, and Gato Amigo not receiving these buffs.
