===Secret Unlockable Cats===
Just like the purchasable Special Cats, both [[Tricycle Cat (Special Cat)|Tricycle Cat]] and [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Flower Cat]] have unused True Forms that are fully functional and cannot be used without modifying the user's save file.

===Cat Bros===
From [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.0 Update|Patch 1.0.0]] to [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.4 Update|Patch 1.0.4]], all of the unused True Forms (excluding Cyperbunk Cat) received a placeholder name and description, that being "@" before being shortly removed in Patch 1.0.5. Funnily enough, this leaves a very unusual oversight with Cat Bros receiving this placeholder, which interestingly enough, allows the player to put it into their formation and have the placeholder sprite summon if they used Cat Bros' "True Form". It does not cost anything to the player can can be summoned immediately, however it does not eat up any deployment cost, allowing the player to spam this unused True Form as much as their heart desires. 

===Cyberpunk Cat===
Unlike the other unused True Forms listed in this section, [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]]'s True Form, Cyberpunk Cat, is left at a broken state. While he can be used in-game via save file editing, he costs 0¢ and has the same recharge time as [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]]. When summoned, he plays through his entire animations list before remaining at his idle animation. The only way he can die naturally without wasting your deployment limit is when a boss wave occurs. 

