===Cat Combos===
There is an unused sprite for [[Cat Combo]]s as well as a question regarding about Cat Combos.

===More Unused Stages===
In the cbs files from both Data.arc and Patch001.arc archives, there is a myriad of unused stages that went unused in the Switch port. A majority of [[:Category:Monthly Events|Monthly Events]], [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone Stages]], Special Cat [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]], [[Deadly Carnival!|Deadly]] [[Deadly Carnival II|Carnival]] stages, Tier 1 and Tier 2 [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stages]], other [[Event Stages]], and Stories of Legend stages that go all the way up to sub-chapter 46, [[Singularityville]].

===Cat Stamp Logins===
This could have been leftover data from importing data from the mobile version when developing the Nintendo Switch version, but there could have been a 30-day login bonus similar to the mobile version which was instead discarded in favor of the Text Speech method to unlock Tricycle Cat.

===Recording Settings===
In a cbs file from the Data.arc archive, there was text mentioning the ability to record a [[Battle|battle]] while playing, which would be saved into the console's album.

===Unused Gacha System Sprites===
In the spritesheet that is used to indicate what rarity was obtained from rolling the Cat Capsule, there is an unused sprite mentioning "Legend" and could have been simply ported from the mobile version. There also exists unused sprites for receiving 1 million XP, guaranteed uber draws, and looking up the event info for each banner.

===Unused Sales Sprites===
Since this version of the game does not use in-app purchases, there are unused sprites promoting sales for Platinum and Rare Tickets, Limited Packs, and a Start Up pack.

===Unused Items===
Catseyes and Catamins are present in the games files as well as leftover sprites for Catamins being available on the Item Store as well.

===Crazed Cats in the Enemy Guide===
A text file that contained descriptions for the enemies encountered in the game, there are slots for the enemy forms of the Crazed Cats albeit with no text. However, there is no mention for the enemy forms of the Manic Cats.
===Unused Missions and Banners===
There are several missions that were added in The Battle Cats Unite for the International Version as well as additional banners that were going to be added to be unlocked.
*The following missions that are unused in the International Version:
**Login to claim Catburger
**Login to claim Driller Cat
**Login to claim Piledriver Cat
**Login to claim Cutter Cat
**Login to claim Backhoe Cat
**Login to claim Miter Saw Cat
*The following banners have been mentioned in the game's files and were mentioned to be planned additions:
**[[Girls & Monsters: Angels of Terror (Gacha Event)|Girls & Monsters: Angels of Terror]]
**[[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES]]
It should be noted that Iron Legion was also mentioned among these files and was the only one of the three that have been fully implemented into the game. The unused missions for the International Version may be future content that will be distributed as Catburger remains to be the only unavailable unit across all three releases for the game.

==Trivia==
*The Battle Cats Unite! would have been the first iteration of The Battle Cats to have [[:Category:Enemy Cats|enemy cats]] (besides major bosses such as [[:Category:Mythic Bosses|Mythic Bosses]], [[Evil Emperor Cat]] and [[Ensanglion the Calamity]]) or seasonal variants appear in the [[Enemy Guide]], however, it seems to have been cut rather early on as the enemy Crazed Cats' description slots have no text and only mention their name.
*Bahamut Cat's awakening stage is ordered in the same category as the [[FINALS WEEK|Go Go Graduates!]] stages when viewing the stage list order text file.

